        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "description": "How long the worst-exposed machine has carried at least one outstanding security patch, counted from the last time it read zero. **This is the elapsed-time question the strategy asks**, and it is the number a maturity-level argument turns on. Capped at 30 days, which is how far back the query looks: a node at the cap has been exposed for at least that long and possibly much longer. Empty means no machine is carrying a security patch at all.",
      "id": 1917725061
    },
