    {
      "title": "Multi-factor authentication",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 16,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 37
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Puppet does not evidence this control on its own.** MFA is enforced by an identity provider, a directory, or a PAM stack, and none of those report to Puppet.\n\nWhat Puppet can show is whether the *configuration* that enables MFA is under management and holding \u2014 PAM, SSSD or an agent's own config, where a site manages them with Puppet. The tile beside this counts resources of those types. **A number here is evidence that the configuration is enforced. It is not evidence that MFA is enabled, and must not be read as such.**"
      },
      "id": 240778605
    },
    {
      "title": "Identity Config Under Management",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 37
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
