    {
      "title": "Application control",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 16,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 53
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Managing packages is not application control, and this board will not claim it is.** The strategy asks whether execution of unapproved software is *prevented* \u2014 AppLocker, WDAC, fapolicyd, SELinux in enforcing mode. Puppet can configure those, and where a site does, the resources appear in the tile beside this.\n\nWhat Puppet knows for certain is which packages are under management, which is software inventory control rather than execution control. Useful, adjacent, and a different claim."
      },
      "id": 98105344
    },
