          "valueSize": 22
        }
      },
      "description": "Windows nodes where Puppet enforces each control at the value it requires, against the node count beside this. **The value is the control, not the key**: a Defender rule set to Audit logs and allows, so it is counted as its own bar rather than folded into the blocked one. Level 1 lives in HKCU and is per user, which is why a node hardened by SCE alone carries none of it.",
      "id": 1602116177
    },
    {
      "title": "What this row cannot tell you",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 68
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Coverage, not conformance.** These bars count nodes where Puppet *declares* the setting, read from the catalogue. They do not read the registry, so they say the estate intends to enforce this and not that the value is currently correct on the machine.\n\n**Every Level 1 macro setting lives in HKCU, and Facter runs as SYSTEM.** A fact reading `HKCU\\Software\\Policies\\...` reads SYSTEM's own empty hive and returns a clean, confident, wrong answer on every node. Conformance needs applied policy state (`registry.pol` or RSoP) and that fact does not exist yet.\n\n**A site enforcing macros through Group Policy or Intune has an equally valid control that Puppet cannot see.** Empty here means Puppet is not the enforcement path. It is not a finding against the control, and no maturity level is being claimed either way."
      },
      "id": 738632515
    },
