    {
      "title": "Regular backups",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 85
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Puppet does not evidence fleet backups, and pdctng's backup metrics are not about the fleet.** `puppet_backup_*` describes the Puppet primary's own PE backup: one server, carrying no node dimension at all. Putting it under this heading would answer a question about the estate with a fact about one machine, so it is deliberately not on this board. It is on PDCTNG Infrastructure Health, where it is honestly labelled.\n\nBackup coverage for the fleet is enforced and evidenced by a backup product, not by Puppet. Where a site manages backup *agents* with Puppet, class adoption would show the agent is installed \u2014 which is evidence the agent is deployed, not that backups are running or restorable."
      },
      "id": 1364923922
    }
  ],
  "description": "What Puppet can evidence against the ACSC Essential Eight, and what it cannot. Evidence of controls under enforcement; not a maturity level assessment."
}
